\cf2 <$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Road-kill pie?\'92 Sarah offered Tony an oozing slice of mostly pastry, gravy and \'85 best not think about it.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Um. No thanks. Where did all this come from?\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Offerings from the Elvi devotees,\'92 said Denver Elvis, who had been lurking unnoticed by the doors to the front parlour. \'91For the Holy Momma. And our talented song-writer.\'92 Denver smiled for Tony.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91I wish you wouldn\'92t call me that,\'92 Sarah grumbled. \'91Or him that.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91What? Talented?\'92 Tony objected.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91He is setting aside the years of great squabbling over 
